From 6b32b68ff66dfc17d31bd5cb3295c1f698a101c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AkiyamaRin <akir1n@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:44:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix: address review findings on the performance patch

- Take the KB lock and the indexing claim inside the protected region and release
  on every path; a configuration error during setup used to leak the lock file with
  a live pid, which wedged the KB until the lock looked stale.
- Make the vector/chunk mismatch guard fail closed in hybrid mode: the misaligned
  vectors no longer reach redundancy scoring, only a warning does.
- Detect truncated sidecars: searchVectorFile reports a short read, and search skips
  that KB's vector half instead of silently pairing what it could read.
- Narrow the no-op update optimisation to skipping the sidecar rewrite only. Symbols,
  counts, source options and status still run, because they derive from the source
  and can change while every chunk hash stays the same (e.g. a renamed heading in a
  too-short-to-chunk section).
- Create idx_chunks_kb_file on every open, not just for fresh databases, so existing
  installations pick it up.
- Make the lock ownership-safe: publish by link() from a written staging file, treat
  unreadable locks as reclaimable only after a grace period, and only delete a lock
  whose token still matches.
- Fix consecutive headings: a heading now owns the lines after it even when the
  preceding section was empty.
- Add regression tests for spans, no-op sidecar reuse, the mismatch guard and the
  cross-process lock.
